---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Short Film Projects
---

<div class="w3-padding-64 w3-content cinematic-projects">
  <h2 class="w3-text-light-grey">Short Film Projects</h2>

  {% for p in (collections.project or []) | reverse %}
    {% if (p.data.section or '').toLowerCase() == 'short film projects' %}
      <div class="film-project w3-margin-bottom">
        <h3 class="w3-text-light-grey" style="margin:18px 0 8px;">{{ p.data.title }}</h3>

        {% if p.data.vimeoId %}
          {# Keep real project IDs. A standalone demonstration can use 76979871. #}
          {% set playerKey = 'cinema-' ~ loop.index %}

          <section
            class="cinema"
            data-cinema
            data-video-id="{{ p.data.vimeoId | escape }}"
            aria-label="{{ p.data.title | escape }} video player"
          >
            <div class="cinema-screen">
              <!-- The iframe is created on demand through the official Player API. -->
              <div class="cinema-video" data-video-layer></div>

              <img
                class="cinema-poster"
                data-poster
                src="/img/optimized/projects/short-film/{{ p.data.vimeoId | escape }}.webp"
                alt=""
                loading="lazy"
                decoding="async"
                width="1920"
                height="1080"
              >

              <div class="cinema-camera-layer" data-camera-layer>
                <button
                  class="cinema-camera"
                  data-camera
                  type="button"
                  aria-label="Play {{ p.data.title | escape }}"
                >
                  <!-- Original vector artwork: two reels, body and lens; no tripod. -->
                  <svg viewBox="0 0 300 210" width="300" height="210" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
                    <defs>
                      <linearGradient id="{{ playerKey }}-metal" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="1">
                        <stop offset="0" stop-color="#f5e6d3"/>
                        <stop offset="0.5" stop-color="#d4a24e"/>
                        <stop offset="1" stop-color="#8b5d28"/>
                      </linearGradient>
                      <radialGradient id="{{ playerKey }}-glass">
                        <stop offset="0" stop-color="#ffd970"/>
                        <stop offset="0.55" stop-color="#8b3a2a"/>
                        <stop offset="1" stop-color="#2a1810"/>
                      </radialGradient>
                    </defs>

                    <!-- Unique IDs prevent collisions between multiple film players. -->
                    <g id="{{ playerKey }}-reel-left" class="cinema-reel">
                      <circle cx="86" cy="58" r="43" fill="url(#{{ playerKey }}-metal)" stroke="#2a1810" stroke-width="5"/>
                      <g fill="#3a2418">
                        <circle cx="86" cy="33" r="10"/>
                        <circle cx="110" cy="58" r="10"/>
                        <circle cx="86" cy="83" r="10"/>
                        <circle cx="62" cy="58" r="10"/>
                      </g>
                      <circle cx="86" cy="58" r="6" fill="#f5e6d3"/>
                    </g>

                    <g id="{{ playerKey }}-reel-right" class="cinema-reel">
                      <circle cx="177" cy="58" r="43" fill="url(#{{ playerKey }}-metal)" stroke="#2a1810" stroke-width="5"/>
                      <g fill="#3a2418">
                        <circle cx="177" cy="33" r="10"/>
                        <circle cx="201" cy="58" r="10"/>
                        <circle cx="177" cy="83" r="10"/>
                        <circle cx="153" cy="58" r="10"/>
                      </g>
                      <circle cx="177" cy="58" r="6" fill="#f5e6d3"/>
                    </g>

                    <rect x="51" y="101" width="162" height="88" rx="17" fill="#3a2418" stroke="url(#{{ playerKey }}-metal)" stroke-width="5"/>
                    <rect x="65" y="115" width="132" height="58" rx="8" fill="#2a1810" stroke="#8b3a2a" stroke-width="2"/>
                    <path d="M213 127 L244 115 L244 175 L213 163 Z" fill="url(#{{ playerKey }}-metal)" stroke="#2a1810" stroke-width="3"/>
                    <ellipse cx="246" cy="145" rx="13" ry="30" fill="url(#{{ playerKey }}-glass)" stroke="#d4a24e" stroke-width="4"/>
                    <ellipse class="cinema-lens-glow" cx="246" cy="145" rx="16" ry="33" fill="#ffd970"/>
                    <ellipse data-lens cx="246" cy="145" rx="3" ry="3" fill="#f5e6d3"/>
                    <path d="M78 146 H148 M78 154 H129" stroke="#d4a24e" stroke-width="3"/>
                    <circle cx="178" cy="143" r="9" fill="#8b3a2a" stroke="#d4a24e" stroke-width="2"/>
                  </svg>
                  <span class="cinema-camera-caption" data-caption>Begin the picture</span>
                </button>
              </div>

              <!-- Transform and opacity animate this isolated transition layer. -->
              <div class="cinema-beam" data-beam aria-hidden="true"></div>

              <a
                class="cinema-credit"
                href="https://vimeo.com/{{ p.data.vimeoId | escape }}"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
                aria-label="Watch this film on Vimeo"
              >vimeo</a>

              <div class="cinema-fallback" data-fallback role="alert" hidden>
                <div>
                  <strong>The picture could not start</strong>
                  <p>We could not load the film. Please check your connection and refresh the page.</p>
                  <a href="https://vimeo.com/{{ p.data.vimeoId | escape }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Watch on Vimeo</a>
                  <button type="button" data-refresh aria-label="Refresh the page">Refresh</button>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Controls remain in document flow to avoid covering narrow videos. -->
            <div class="cinema-controls" data-controls aria-label="Film controls" hidden>
              <input
                class="cinema-progress"
                data-progress
                type="range"
                min="0"
                max="1000"
                step="1"
                value="0"
                aria-label="Seek through the film"
                aria-valuetext="00:00 of 00:00"
                disabled
              >

              <div class="cinema-control-row">
                <button type="button" data-toggle aria-label="Play film">▶</button>
                <button type="button" data-replay aria-label="Replay film">↺</button>
                <button type="button" data-sound aria-label="Unmute film">Unmute</button>
                <span class="cinema-time" data-time aria-live="off">00:00 / 00:00</span>

                <label>
                  <span>Speed</span>
                  <select data-speed aria-label="Playback speed">
                    <option value="0.5">0.5x</option>
                    <option value="1" selected>1x</option>
                    <option value="1.5">1.5x</option>
                  </select>
                </label>

                <label>
                  <span>Quality</span>
                  <select data-quality aria-label="Video quality" disabled>
                    <option value="auto">Auto</option>
                  </select>
                </label>
              </div>
            </div>

            <p class="cinema-status" data-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>

            <noscript>
              <p><a href="https://vimeo.com/{{ p.data.vimeoId | escape }}">Watch this film on Vimeo</a>. JavaScript is required for the custom player.</p>
            </noscript>
          </section>
        {% endif %}

        {% if p.templateContent %}
          <div class="w3-text-grey" style="line-height:1.7;">
            {{ p.templateContent | safe }}
          </div>
        {% endif %}

        <hr class="w3-opacity">
      </div>
    {% endif %}
  {% endfor %}
</div>

<style>
/* Scope every rule to this component instead of changing shared site styles. */
.cinematic-projects .cinema {
  --cinema-brown: #2a1810;
  --cinema-panel: #3a2418;
  --cinema-gold: #d4a24e;
  --cinema-cream: #f5e6d3;
  position: relative;
  isolation: isolate;
  margin-bottom: 16px;
  color: var(--cinema-cream);
  background: var(--cinema-brown);
  border: 1px solid #8b5d28;
  border-radius: 16px;
  overflow: hidden;
}

.cinema [hidden] {
  display: none !important;
}

.cinema .cinema-screen {
  position: relative;
  aspect-ratio: 16 / 9;
  overflow: hidden;
  isolation: isolate;
  background: radial-gradient(ellipse at center, #59402a, #2a1810 70%);
}

.cinema .cinema-video,
.cinema .cinema-video iframe,
.cinema .cinema-poster,
.cinema .cinema-camera-layer {
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
}

.cinema .cinema-video {
  z-index: 1;
}

.cinema .cinema-video iframe {
  border: 0;
  pointer-events: none;
}

.cinema .cinema-poster {
  z-index: 2;
  object-fit: cover;
  opacity: 0.5;
  transition: opacity 400ms ease-out;
}

.cinema.is-started .cinema-poster {
  opacity: 0;
  pointer-events: none;
}

.cinema .cinema-camera-layer {
  z-index: 10;
  display: grid;
  place-items: center;
  background: linear-gradient(0deg, #2a181066, transparent);
  transition: opacity 400ms ease-out;
}

.cinema.is-launching .cinema-camera-layer,
.cinema.is-started .cinema-camera-layer {
  opacity: 0;
  pointer-events: none;
}

.cinema .cinema-camera {
  display: grid;
  justify-items: center;
  width: clamp(140px, 32%, 300px);
  padding: 0;
  border: 0;
  background: none;
  color: var(--cinema-cream);
  cursor: pointer;
}

.cinema .cinema-camera svg {
  display: block;
  width: 100%;
  height: auto;
}

.cinema .cinema-camera-caption {
  font-family: Georgia, serif;
  font-size: clamp(12px, 1.5vw, 17px);
  letter-spacing: 0.12em;
  text-shadow: 0 2px 4px #000;
}

.cinema .cinema-reel {
  transform-box: fill-box;
  transform-origin: center;
  transform: rotate(0deg);
  transition: transform 600ms ease-out;
}

.cinema .cinema-lens-glow {
  opacity: 0;
  transition: opacity 600ms ease-out;
  isolation: isolate;
}

@media (hover: hover) {
  .cinema .cinema-screen:hover .cinema-reel {
    transform: rotate(360deg);
    will-change: transform;
  }

  .cinema .cinema-screen:hover .cinema-lens-glow {
    opacity: 0.85;
  }
}

.cinema .cinema-camera:focus-visible .cinema-reel {
  transform: rotate(360deg);
  will-change: transform;
}

.cinema .cinema-camera:focus-visible .cinema-lens-glow {
  opacity: 0.85;
}

.cinema button:focus-visible,
.cinema a:focus-visible,
.cinema select:focus-visible,
.cinema input:focus-visible {
  outline: 3px solid #ffd970;
  outline-offset: 3px;
}

.cinema .cinema-beam {
  position: absolute;
  z-index: 20;
  pointer-events: none;
  border-radius: 50%;
  background: radial-gradient(circle, #fff3c4 0%, #ffd970 45%, #d4a24e 75%, #d4a24e00 100%);
  opacity: 0;
  transform: translate(-50%, -50%) scale(0);
  isolation: isolate;
}

.cinema .cinema-credit {
  position: absolute;
  right: 12px;
  bottom: 10px;
  z-index: 25;
  color: #fff;
  font-size: 10px;
  font-style: italic;
  font-weight: bold;
  text-decoration: none;
  opacity: 0.4;
  transition: opacity 200ms ease;
}

.cinema .cinema-credit:hover,
.cinema .cinema-credit:focus-visible {
  opacity: 1;
}

.cinema .cinema-controls {
  position: relative;
  z-index: 30;
  background: linear-gradient(#3a2418, #2a1810);
  border-top: 1px solid #8b5d28;
  padding: 8px 12px 12px;
  transition: opacity 220ms ease;
}

.cinema.controls-idle .cinema-controls {
  opacity: 0;
  pointer-events: none;
}

.cinema.controls-idle .cinema-controls:focus-within {
  opacity: 1;
  pointer-events: auto;
}

.cinema .cinema-progress {
  position: relative;
  z-index: 30;
  display: block;
  width: 100%;
  min-height: 24px;
  margin: 0 0 6px;
  accent-color: var(--cinema-gold);
  cursor: pointer;
}

.cinema .cinema-control-row {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 8px;
}

.cinema .cinema-control-row button,
.cinema .cinema-control-row select,
.cinema .cinema-fallback button {
  min-height: 44px;
  padding: 6px 10px;
  border: 1px solid #8b5d28;
  border-radius: 6px;
  color: var(--cinema-cream);
  background: var(--cinema-panel);
  font: inherit;
  cursor: pointer;
}

.cinema .cinema-control-row button {
  min-width: 44px;
}

.cinema button:disabled,
.cinema select:disabled,
.cinema input:disabled {
  opacity: 0.55;
  cursor: default;
}

.cinema .cinema-control-row label {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 5px;
  font-size: 12px;
}

.cinema .cinema-time {
  margin-right: auto;
  font-size: 12px;
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  white-space: nowrap;
}

.cinema .cinema-status {
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0 12px;
  font-size: 13px;
}

.cinema .cinema-status:not(:empty) {
  padding-top: 8px;
  padding-bottom: 8px;
}

.cinema .cinema-fallback {
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  z-index: 50;
  display: grid;
  place-items: center;
  overflow: auto;
  padding: 18px;
  background: #2a1810b8;
  text-align: center;
}

.cinema .cinema-fallback > div {
  max-width: 440px;
}

.cinema .cinema-fallback a {
  display: inline-block;
  margin: 8px;
  color: #ffd970;
}

.cinema.has-error .cinema-poster {
  opacity: 0.65;
}

.cinema.has-error .cinema-camera-layer {
  visibility: hidden;
}

@media (max-width: 480px) {
  .cinema .cinema-control-row {
    gap: 6px;
  }

  .cinema .cinema-control-row label {
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .cinema .cinema-fallback {
    font-size: 12px;
    padding: 10px;
  }

  .cinema .cinema-fallback p {
    margin: 6px 0;
  }
}

@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .cinema .cinema-reel,
  .cinema .cinema-camera:focus-visible .cinema-reel,
  .cinema .cinema-screen:hover .cinema-reel {
    transform: none;
    transition: none;
    will-change: auto;
  }

  .cinema .cinema-beam {
    display: none;
  }

  .cinema .cinema-poster,
  .cinema .cinema-camera-layer,
  .cinema .cinema-lens-glow,
  .cinema .cinema-controls,
  .cinema .cinema-credit {
    transition: none;
  }
}
</style>

<script>
(function () {
  'use strict';

  // Share one SDK download across all film instances on this page.
  let sdkPromise;

  function loadVimeoSDK() {
    if (window.Vimeo && window.Vimeo.Player) {
      return Promise.resolve(window.Vimeo);
    }

    if (!sdkPromise) {
      sdkPromise = new Promise(function (resolve, reject) {
        const script = document.createElement('script');
        const timeout = window.setTimeout(function () {
          reject(new Error('Vimeo SDK loading timed out.'));
        }, 20000);

        script.src = 'https://player.vimeo.com/api/player.js';
        script.async = true;
        script.onload = function () {
          window.clearTimeout(timeout);
          if (window.Vimeo && window.Vimeo.Player) {
            resolve(window.Vimeo);
          } else {
            reject(new Error('Vimeo SDK is unavailable.'));
          }
        };
        script.onerror = function () {
          window.clearTimeout(timeout);
          reject(new Error('Vimeo SDK could not be loaded.'));
        };
        document.head.appendChild(script);
      });
    }

    return sdkPromise;
  }

  function withTimeout(promise, milliseconds) {
    return new Promise(function (resolve, reject) {
      const timer = window.setTimeout(function () {
        reject(new Error('The player did not respond in time.'));
      }, milliseconds);

      Promise.resolve(promise).then(function (value) {
        window.clearTimeout(timer);
        resolve(value);
      }, function (error) {
        window.clearTimeout(timer);
        reject(error);
      });
    });
  }

  function formatTime(seconds) {
    const safe = Math.max(0, Math.floor(Number(seconds) || 0));
    const hours = Math.floor(safe / 3600);
    const minutes = Math.floor((safe % 3600) / 60);
    const remainder = safe % 60;
    const short = String(minutes).padStart(2, '0') + ':' + String(remainder).padStart(2, '0');
    return hours ? hours + ':' + short : short;
  }

  function initialize() {
    document.querySelectorAll('[data-cinema]').forEach(function (root) {
      if (root.dataset.initialized) return;
      root.dataset.initialized = 'true';

      const find = function (name) {
        return root.querySelector('[data-' + name + ']');
      };

      const screen = root.querySelector('.cinema-screen');
      const camera = find('camera');
      const cameraLayer = find('camera-layer');
      const lens = find('lens');
      const caption = find('caption');
      const beam = find('beam');
      const poster = find('poster');
      const controls = find('controls');
      const toggle = find('toggle');
      const replay = find('replay');
      const sound = find('sound');
      const speed = find('speed');
      const quality = find('quality');
      const progress = find('progress');
      const time = find('time');
      const status = find('status');
      const fallback = find('fallback');
      const reducedMotion = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)');
      const touchCapable = 'ontouchstart' in window || navigator.maxTouchPoints > 0;

      let player;
      let preparation;
      let ready = false;
      let failed = false;
      let started = false;
      let launching = false;
      let paused = true;
      let muted = true;
      let duration = 0;
      let current = 0;
      let lastRate = '1';
      let lastQuality = 'auto';
      let lastTouch = touchCapable && window.matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches;
      let hideTimer;
      let revealTimer;
      let beamAnimation;
      let seekEditing = false;

      function showControls() {
        root.classList.remove('controls-idle');
        window.clearTimeout(hideTimer);

        if (!started || paused || failed) return;

        hideTimer = window.setTimeout(function () {
          if (!controls.contains(document.activeElement) && !paused && !seekEditing) {
            root.classList.add('controls-idle');
          }
        }, 2800);
      }

      function setPaused(value) {
        paused = value;
        toggle.textContent = value ? '▶' : '❚❚';
        toggle.setAttribute('aria-label', value ? 'Play film' : 'Pause film');
        showControls();
      }

      function setMuted(value) {
        muted = value;
        sound.textContent = value ? 'Unmute' : 'Mute';
        sound.setAttribute('aria-label', value ? 'Unmute film' : 'Mute film');
      }

      function updateTime() {
        time.textContent = formatTime(current) + ' / ' + formatTime(duration);
        progress.disabled = duration <= 0;
        if (!seekEditing) {
          progress.value = duration > 0 ? Math.round(current / duration * 1000) : 0;
        }
        progress.setAttribute('aria-valuetext', formatTime(current) + ' of ' + formatTime(duration));
      }

      function fail(error) {
        if (failed) return;
        failed = true;
        launching = false;
        window.clearTimeout(hideTimer);
        window.clearTimeout(revealTimer);
        if (beamAnimation) beamAnimation.cancel();
        beam.style.willChange = 'auto';
        root.classList.add('has-error');
        root.classList.remove('is-launching', 'controls-idle');
        controls.hidden = true;
        camera.disabled = true;
        fallback.hidden = false;
        status.textContent = '';
        if (player) player.pause().catch(function () {});
        console.warn('Cinematic Vimeo player:', error);
        fallback.querySelector('a').focus({ preventScroll: true });
      }

      function notify(message, error) {
        status.textContent = message;
        showControls();
        if (error) console.warn('Cinematic Vimeo control:', error);
      }

      async function loadQualities() {
        try {
          const options = await withTimeout(player.getQualities(), 8000);
          if (failed || !Array.isArray(options) || !options.length) return;

          quality.replaceChildren(new Option('Auto', 'auto'));
          const seen = new Set(['auto']);
          options.forEach(function (option) {
            if (!option || !option.id || seen.has(String(option.id))) return;
            const id = String(option.id);
            seen.add(id);
            quality.add(new Option(String(option.label || id), id));
          });

          try {
            const active = await withTimeout(player.getQuality(), 8000);
            if (seen.has(String(active))) {
              quality.value = String(active);
              lastQuality = String(active);
            }
          } catch (error) {
            lastQuality = 'auto';
          }

          quality.disabled = quality.options.length < 2;
        } catch (error) {
          // The disabled Auto option remains truthful when selection is unsupported.
          quality.disabled = true;
        }
      }

      function prepare() {
        if (preparation) return preparation;

        preparation = (async function () {
          const Vimeo = await loadVimeoSDK();
          if (failed) return;

          const videoId = String(root.dataset.videoId || '');
          if (!/^\d+$/.test(videoId)) {
            throw new Error('The project Vimeo ID is invalid.');
          }

          const iframe = document.createElement('iframe');
          iframe.src = 'https://player.vimeo.com/video/' + videoId +
            '?background=1&autoplay=0&loop=0&byline=0&title=0&portrait=0&controls=0&muted=1&playsinline=1&keyboard=0';
          iframe.title = 'Vimeo film';
          iframe.allow = 'autoplay; fullscreen; picture-in-picture; encrypted-media';
          iframe.allowFullscreen = true;
          iframe.tabIndex = -1;
          find('video-layer').appendChild(iframe);

          player = new Vimeo.Player(iframe);

          player.on('play', function () {
            setPaused(false);
          });

          player.on('pause', function () {
            setPaused(true);
          });

          player.on('ended', function () {
            setPaused(true);
            current = duration;
            updateTime();
          });

          player.on('timeupdate', function (event) {
            current = Number(event.seconds) || 0;
            duration = Number(event.duration) || duration;
            updateTime();
          });

          player.on('durationchange', function (event) {
            duration = Number(event.duration) || 0;
            updateTime();
          });

          player.on('playbackratechange', function (event) {
            lastRate = String(event.playbackRate);
            speed.value = lastRate;
          });

          player.on('qualitychange', function (event) {
            if (!event || !event.id) return;
            lastQuality = String(event.id);
            quality.value = lastQuality;
          });

          player.on('volumechange', function (event) {
            setMuted(Boolean(event.muted) || event.volume === 0);
          });

          player.on('bufferstart', function () {
            if (started) status.textContent = 'Buffering the picture.';
          });

          player.on('bufferend', function () {
            if (status.textContent === 'Buffering the picture.') status.textContent = '';
          });

          player.on('error', function (error) {
            // Optional control failures must not replace a playable film.
            if (error && [
              'setQuality', 'getQuality', 'getQualities',
              'setPlaybackRate', 'setCurrentTime', 'setMuted', 'setVolume'
            ].indexOf(error.method) !== -1) return;
            fail(error);
          });

          await withTimeout(player.ready(), 20000);
          if (failed) return;
          ready = true;

          player.getDuration().then(function (value) {
            duration = Number(value) || 0;
            updateTime();
          }).catch(function () {});

          player.getMuted().then(setMuted).catch(function () {});
          loadQualities();
        })().catch(function (error) {
          fail(error);
        });

        return preparation;
      }

      function reveal() {
        if (failed) return;
        started = true;
        launching = false;
        root.classList.remove('is-launching');
        root.classList.add('is-started');
        cameraLayer.hidden = true;
        controls.hidden = false;
        caption.textContent = 'Begin the picture';
        status.textContent = '';
        showControls();
        if (document.activeElement === camera) {
          toggle.focus({ preventScroll: true });
        }
      }

      function animateLaunch() {
        if (reducedMotion.matches) {
          reveal();
          return;
        }

        // Read geometry together, then write setup dimensions only once.
        const bounds = screen.getBoundingClientRect();
        const lensBounds = lens.getBoundingClientRect();
        const x = lensBounds.left + lensBounds.width / 2 - bounds.left;
        const y = lensBounds.top + lensBounds.height / 2 - bounds.top;
        const radius = Math.hypot(
          Math.max(x, bounds.width - x),
          Math.max(y, bounds.height - y)
        );
        const milliseconds = lastTouch ? 450 : 900;

        beam.style.left = x + 'px';
        beam.style.top = y + 'px';
        beam.style.width = radius * 4 + 'px';
        beam.style.height = radius * 4 + 'px';
        beam.style.willChange = 'transform, opacity';

        // One deliberate layout flush establishes the initial animation state.
        void beam.offsetWidth;

        beamAnimation = beam.animate([
          { offset: 0, opacity: 0, transform: 'translate(-50%, -50%) scale(0)' },
          { offset: 0.55, opacity: 1, transform: 'translate(-50%, -50%) scale(1)' },
          { offset: 1, opacity: 0, transform: 'translate(-50%, -50%) scale(1)' }
        ], {
          duration: milliseconds,
          easing: 'ease-in-out'
        });

        root.classList.add('is-launching');

        // Reveal the moving picture while the beam still masks the change.
        revealTimer = window.setTimeout(reveal, milliseconds * 0.55);
        beamAnimation.finished.then(function () {
          beam.style.willChange = 'auto';
        }).catch(function () {
          beam.style.willChange = 'auto';
        });
      }

      async function launch() {
        if (launching || started || failed) return;
        launching = true;
        camera.disabled = true;
        caption.textContent = 'Preparing the picture';
        status.textContent = 'Preparing the film.';

        await prepare();
        if (failed || !ready) return;

        try {
          // Muted playback survives the asynchronous SDK load on touch browsers.
          await withTimeout(player.play(), 20000);
          if (failed) return;
          camera.disabled = false;
          animateLaunch();
        } catch (error) {
          fail(error);
        }
      }

      root.addEventListener('pointerdown', function (event) {
        lastTouch = event.pointerType === 'touch';
        showControls();
      }, { passive: true });

      root.addEventListener('touchstart', function () {
        lastTouch = true;
        showControls();
      }, { passive: true });

      root.addEventListener('keydown', function () {
        lastTouch = false;
        showControls();
      });

      root.addEventListener('pointermove', showControls, { passive: true });
      root.addEventListener('focusin', showControls);
      root.addEventListener('focusout', function () {
        window.setTimeout(showControls, 0);
      });

      camera.addEventListener('click', launch);
      find('refresh').addEventListener('click', function () {
        window.location.reload();
      });

      poster.addEventListener('error', function () {
        poster.hidden = true;
      });

      toggle.addEventListener('click', async function () {
        if (!ready || failed) return;
        toggle.disabled = true;
        try {
          const isPaused = await withTimeout(player.getPaused(), 8000);
          await withTimeout(isPaused ? player.play() : player.pause(), 15000);
        } catch (error) {
          notify('Playback could not be changed. Please try again.', error);
        } finally {
          toggle.disabled = false;
        }
      });

      replay.addEventListener('click', async function () {
        replay.disabled = true;
        try {
          await withTimeout(player.setCurrentTime(0).then(function () {
            return player.play();
          }), 15000);
        } catch (error) {
          notify('The film could not be replayed. Please try again.', error);
        } finally {
          replay.disabled = false;
        }
      });

      sound.addEventListener('click', async function () {
        sound.disabled = true;
        try {
          await withTimeout(player.setMuted(!muted), 8000);
          setMuted(await withTimeout(player.getMuted(), 8000));
        } catch (error) {
          notify('Sound could not be changed. Please use your device sound controls.', error);
        } finally {
          sound.disabled = false;
        }
      });

      speed.addEventListener('change', async function () {
        const previous = lastRate;
        speed.disabled = true;
        try {
          const actual = await withTimeout(player.setPlaybackRate(Number(speed.value)), 8000);
          lastRate = String(actual);
          speed.value = lastRate;
          status.textContent = '';
        } catch (error) {
          speed.value = previous;
          notify('This film does not support the selected playback speed.', error);
        } finally {
          speed.disabled = false;
        }
      });

      quality.addEventListener('change', async function () {
        const previous = lastQuality;
        quality.disabled = true;
        try {
          const actual = await withTimeout(player.setQuality(quality.value), 10000);
          lastQuality = String(actual);
          quality.value = lastQuality;
          status.textContent = '';
        } catch (error) {
          quality.value = previous;
          notify('Manual quality selection is unavailable for this film.', error);
        } finally {
          quality.disabled = quality.options.length < 2;
        }
      });

      progress.addEventListener('input', function () {
        seekEditing = true;
        showControls();
        const preview = duration * Number(progress.value) / 1000;
        time.textContent = formatTime(preview) + ' / ' + formatTime(duration);
        progress.setAttribute('aria-valuetext', formatTime(preview) + ' of ' + formatTime(duration));
      });

      progress.addEventListener('change', async function () {
        try {
          current = await withTimeout(
            player.setCurrentTime(duration * Number(progress.value) / 1000),
            10000
          );
        } catch (error) {
          notify('Seeking failed. Please try again.', error);
        } finally {
          seekEditing = false;
          updateTime();
          showControls();
        }
      });

      progress.addEventListener('blur', function () {
        seekEditing = false;
        updateTime();
      });

      reducedMotion.addEventListener('change', function (event) {
        if (event.matches && beamAnimation) {
          beamAnimation.cancel();
          window.clearTimeout(revealTimer);
          if (launching && ready && !paused) reveal();
        }
      });
    });
  }

  if (document.readyState === 'loading') {
    document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', initialize, { once: true });
  } else {
    initialize();
  }
})();
</script>

{#
SERVER-SIDE TRANSCODING NOTES

The commands below belong on a server with FFmpeg installed.
They are documentation, not browser code or template execution.

Vimeo generates and serves its own adaptive renditions.
The Vimeo quality menu only controls renditions exposed by Vimeo.
A custom HLS master playlist cannot be assigned to a Vimeo iframe.
Self-hosted HLS requires a separate HTML video player and hosting setup.

This example expects a source with video and audio.
It produces padded 1080p, 720p and 480p renditions at 30 frames per second.
Avoid upscaling low-resolution sources in production.

mkdir -p hls/1080p hls/720p hls/480p

ffmpeg -i input.mp4 \
  -filter_complex "[0:v]fps=30,split=3[v1][v2][v3];[v1]scale=1920:1080:force_original_aspect_ratio=decrease,pad=1920:1080:(ow-iw)/2:(oh-ih)/2,setsar=1[o1];[v2]scale=1280:720:force_original_aspect_ratio=decrease,pad=1280:720:(ow-iw)/2:(oh-ih)/2,setsar=1[o2];[v3]scale=854:480:force_original_aspect_ratio=decrease,pad=854:480:(ow-iw)/2:(oh-ih)/2,setsar=1[o3]" \
  -map "[o1]" -map 0:a:0 \
  -map "[o2]" -map 0:a:0 \
  -map "[o3]" -map 0:a:0 \
  -c:v libx264 -preset medium -pix_fmt yuv420p \
  -g 180 -keyint_min 180 -sc_threshold 0 \
  -force_key_frames "expr:gte(t,n_forced*6)" \
  -b:v:0 5000k -maxrate:v:0 5350k -bufsize:v:0 7500k \
  -b:v:1 2800k -maxrate:v:1 3000k -bufsize:v:1 4200k \
  -b:v:2 1400k -maxrate:v:2 1500k -bufsize:v:2 2100k \
  -c:a aac -ar 48000 -ac 2 \
  -b:a:0 192k -b:a:1 128k -b:a:2 96k \
  -f hls -hls_time 6 -hls_playlist_type vod \
  -hls_flags independent_segments \
  -hls_segment_filename "hls/%v/segment_%05d.ts" \
  -master_pl_name master.m3u8 \
  -var_stream_map "v:0,a:0,name:1080p v:1,a:1,name:720p v:2,a:2,name:480p" \
  "hls/%v/index.m3u8"

Serve m3u8 files with Content-Type application/vnd.apple.mpegurl.
Serve ts files with Content-Type video/mp2t.
Use HTTPS and configure CORS when the player and media use different origins.
Validate all renditions before publishing the master playlist.
Adaptive bitrate can reduce buffering but cannot guarantee uninterrupted playback.
#}
